 HISTORY                                                            44 1451
 -------                                                            44 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics    44 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The          44 1451
 inelastic scattering cross section libraries for C in 3C-SiC       44 1451
 were fully developed using ab-initio lattice dynamics (AILD)       44 1451
 methods [1]. The phonon DOS used in this evaluation was            44 1451
 generated using an AILD model for 3C-SiC [2]. The trigonal         44 1451
 structure, belonging to the F-43m space group (#216), was          44 1451
 modeled in VASP [3-5] using the GGA exchange-correlation           44 1451
 functional with a 900eV plane-wave cutoff energy and a 3x3x3       44 1451
 Monkhorst-Pack k-mesh. The phonon density of states was            44 1451
 generated using a 3x3x3 supercell in PHONON [6] via the            44 1451
 dynamical matrix method. For this evaluation, the energy grid      44 1451
 resolution was increased in the PHONON DOS evaluation. Nine        44 1451
 temperatures are available in this library. The Full Law           44 1451
 Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) was used to produce MT     44 1451
 = 2 (coherent) and MT = 4 data [7]. By convention, MAT=44 and      44 1451
 ZA=144 are used for C in 3C-SiC.                                   44 1451
                                                                    44 1451
 The silicon carbide evluation improved the ENDF/B-VIII.0           44 1451
 evaluation with key updates: (1) lattice constants from            44 1451
 experimental values were used [8], (2) the DOS was improved        44 1451
 with increased resolution, and (3) the coherent elastic was        44 1451
 updated to the cubic evaluation in FLASSH [7].                     44 1451
